    "body": "**factory · triage → needs_info** · claude-sonnet-5 · $0.32 · 1m\nNot reproduced: the report gives no CSV sample, command, column name, or the two numbers being compared (tally's output vs finance's figure), so there's no way to tell whether this is a code bug (e.g. currency formatting like \"$1,234.56\" or \"(12.34)\" that `float()` can't parse, float-summation rounding at scale, duplicate rows) or a data/scope mismatch (finance excluding voided/refunded rows tally includes, a different date range, wrong `--column`). total() in src/tally/__init__.py:11-15 is a straightforward float sum with no such handling either way. Need: the exact `tally` invocation used, the input CSV (or a representative sample), tally's printed total, and finance's total for the same data.\n\nImplementation area: src/tally/__init__.py total(). Prior related closed issue #2 fixed blank-cell crashes; open issue #5 (make tally faster, parked) and #4 (--group-by/--format spec) are unrelated but touch the same file.\n<!-- factory:run {\"verdict\":\"needs_info\",\"station\":\"triage\",\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"turns\":14,\"session_id\":\"5dd88755-34c2-4f45-b09b-239d2aeab227\",\"cost_usd\":0.3225,\"duration_ms\":67517,\"ts\":\"2026-09-13T03:16:15Z\",\"run_url\":null} -->",
