    "body": "**factory · triage → automatable** · claude-sonnet-5 · $0.30 · 1m · [run](https://github.com/tianchi-fetch/factory-sandbox/actions/runs/34764133807)\nReproduced: `float()` in `tally()` can't parse currency-formatted cells like `$1,234.56` (dollar sign + thousands comma), so the reporter's finance export errors out instead of summing to 1246.56. Fix is bounded: strip `$` and thousands `,` before `float(cell)` in `cell_values()`.\n\nImplementation area: `cell_values()` in src/tally/__init__.py (~lines 44-53), used by both `total()` and `tally()`. Keep the existing \"fail loudly with row number\" behavior for genuinely unparseable values (e.g. don't add speculative support for parenthesized negatives or non-USD symbols — not evidenced by the report; if real data needs that, a new issue will surface it). Preserve invariant 3 (group-by same column as sum column groups by raw, unmodified cell text) — only the value used for summing should be stripped, not the group key. Add a test using the reporter's exact sample (`$1,234.56`, `$12.00`, blank) asserting total 1246.56. No related open issues/PRs duplicate this; issue #5 (perf, parked) and #4 (--group-by/--format, has its own spec under specs/4-group-by-and-format/) touch the same file but are unrelated.\n<!-- factory:run {\"verdict\":\"automatable\",\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"duration_ms\":65469,\"turns\":10,\"ts\":\"2026-09-13T14:58:34Z\",\"run_url\":\"https://github.com/tianchi-fetch/factory-sandbox/actions/runs/34764133807\",\"head\":null,\"session_id\":\"e31f44c3-47d6-46e8-80ff-c285b0f45144\",\"station\":\"triage\",\"cost_usd\":0.3033} -->",
